Package: sparsediff
Type: Package
Title: R Interface to the SparseDiffEngine Sparse Differentiation Backend
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Balasubramanian", "Narasimhan", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "naras@stanford.edu"),
    person("Charlie", "Vanaret", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = "Author of the bundled SparseDiffEngine C library"),
    person(family = "SparseDifferentiation contributors", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = "SparseDiffEngine C library"))
Description: R bindings to the 'SparseDiffEngine' C library, the sparse
    Jacobian and Hessian differentiation backend used by 'CVXPY' for its
    Disciplined Nonlinear Programming (DNLP) extension. Provides low-level
    routines for building nonlinear expression graphs and evaluating sparse
    derivatives, intended as a backend for higher-level modeling layers such
    as 'CVXR'. This package is the R analog of the 'sparsediffpy' Python
    package and wraps the same C library.
License: Apache License (== 2.0)
URL: https://github.com/bnaras/sparsediff
BugReports: https://github.com/bnaras/sparsediff/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: A BLAS library (provided by R); the bundled
    SparseDiffEngine sources are built from C99.
LinkingTo:
    cpp11
Suggests:
    cpp11
NeedsCompilation: yes
